lane: fifo-array-front
why: the segmented buffer's real idea is not mutability, it is that
  ELEMENTS LIVE IN ARRAYS. That transfers to a persistent structure
  intact: make Fifo's front an immutable array plus a start index.
  Each state version keeps its own index, the array is never mutated,
  so persistence and STM composability are untouched.
  What it buys: the refill step (front empty, back must be turned
  round) allocates ONE object instead of n cons cells; the elementwise
  dequeue becomes index arithmetic instead of pointer chasing; a
  batched take from the front becomes an array copy.
  Honest about size: the batched path already builds no reversed list
  (fill walks the back writing descending), so the gain there is
  locality only. The elementwise path is where the tuple and the
  amortized reverse still are.
  Both lanes already lead zio (114.5 vs 123.8 chunked, 223.4 vs 302.0
  elementwise), so this is finishing the structure, not closing a gap.
  Land only if measured faster; revert if not.
